      "worked": "The semicircle has centre at the origin. At $x=2$, its intersection is $(2,2)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}r&=\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}\\\\y&=\\sqrt{8-2^2}=2\\end{align*}$$\nThe radius to $(2,2)$ makes equal angles with the positive coordinate axes. The sector beside the positive $y$-axis therefore has angle\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=\\frac{\\pi}{4}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe required region consists of this sector and a right triangle with perpendicular sides $2$ and $2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac12(2\\sqrt{2})^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)+\\frac12(2)(2)\\\\A&=\\pi+2\\text{ square units}.\\end{align*}$$",
